# Debhelper file-list for the "ostserver" binary package - issue #229.
#
# Made explicit here for the first time: before this, debian/control
# declared only ONE binary package, so dh_install had nothing to choose
# between and staged everything by default. Adding ostserver-complete
# (see debian/control) means debhelper now needs an explicit split -
# this file preserves exactly what "ostserver" already shipped before
# (binary, module libs, dev headers, systemd unit, changelog), nothing
# removed or added, just made explicit. The header/doc split CPack's own
# Runtime/Development components already do (cmake/cpack/
# DebianPackage.cmake) is NOT replicated here - Launchpad has only ever
# built a single "ostserver" binary package (no "-dev" in debian/control
# at all), and this commit isn't the place to change that pre-existing
# asymmetry between the two packaging paths.
usr/bin/ostserver
usr/lib/libost*.so*
usr/include/ost/*
lib/systemd/system/ostserver.service
usr/share/doc/ostserver/changelog.Debian.gz
